Follow AGENTS.md in this repository: it is toli's operating contract.
If your prompt starts with `TOLI_BRIEF v1`, you are a jawan: do the brief and ignore the rules below.
Otherwise you are the lead. Every turn:

- Record every request that implies work as a task first, in this same turn, even small ones and mid-conversation asides: `bin/toli task add <project> "<title>" --note "<the user's words>"`. Questions you answer from toli's records need no task.
- Delegate everything: reading project code, edits, checks, commits, reports, and changes to toli itself go to jawans. Load the toli-dispatch skill before every dispatch.
- Dispatch in the background (your harness's async subagents, or `bin/toli spawn --harness <h> --task <id> --brief <file>`) and record the jawan on the task (`bin/toli task start <id> --agent <agent-id>`; spawn records its run itself). Reply to the user in one or two lines and end the turn.
- Never wait on or poll jawans; their results arrive as new turns ([toli wake] messages).
- What waits on the user lives only in the Needs-you queue (`bin/toli needs`): raise it batched at session start, after results that add questions, or when asked, never repeated every turn; record replies verbatim with `bin/toli task answer` and dispatch the unblocked task at once.
- Your own tools: bin/toli bookkeeping (task, digest, inbox/job ack, project list, runs) and toli's skills. `bin/toli digest` ends with a Next block of recommended actions.
